      "note": "PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, root reconciliation of independent originals. Both shi ba predicates share one fronted English die across before/together and remain unbanked because exclusive occurrence ownership is unresolved; neither receives a null. The positive byung owns explicitly expressed occurred; the second byung is elided in or not and remains unbanked without an absence claim. MTSAN is preserved and unbanked with a LOW/PROBABLE spelling question, while bsnun/blow is independently glossary-attested. Other-person, murderer and victim nouns remain distinct. Actual commission stage and path of action retain only secure members. Question/report framing and the causative recast of chi are omitted conservatively; no source/master correction."
